# CI / CD Rules — SimpleImageConverter

## Runner OS Constraints

- Windows builds must use `runs-on: windows-latest`.
- Linux builds use `runs-on: ubuntu-latest` with explicit system library install.
- macOS builds and signed releases must use `runs-on: macos-latest`.
- Never assume the runner matches any local dev machine.

## No Local Paths

Workflow files and scripts must never contain:
- `/Users/` paths
- `C:\Users\` paths
- `/home/<specific-username>/` paths

Use `$GITHUB_WORKSPACE`, `$RUNNER_TEMP`, or relative paths from repo root.

## CI Pattern — Core Rust Jobs

```yaml
- name: Setup Rust
  uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable
  with:
    toolchain: stable
    components: rustfmt, clippy

- name: Cache cargo
  uses: actions/cache@v4
  with:
    path: |
      ~/.cargo/bin/
      ~/.cargo/registry/index/
      ~/.cargo/registry/cache/
      ~/.cargo/git/db/
      target/
    key: ${{ runner.os }}-cargo-${{ hashFiles('**/Cargo.lock') }}

- name: Build
  run: cargo build --workspace --release

- name: Test
  run: cargo test --workspace

- name: Format check
  run: cargo fmt --check

- name: Clippy
  run: cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings

- name: Security audit
  run: cargo audit
```

## Linux System Dependencies in CI

When running on `ubuntu-latest`, always install egui/eframe system deps first:

```yaml
- name: Install Linux system dependencies
  run: |
    sudo apt-get update
    sudo apt-get install -y \
      libxcb-render0-dev \
      libxcb-shape0-dev \
      libxcb-xfixes0-dev \
      libxkbcommon-dev \
      libssl-dev \
      pkg-config
```

## Matrix Strategy for Cross-Platform Builds

```yaml
strategy:
  matrix:
    os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest, macos-latest]
runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
```

When using a matrix, install Linux system deps conditionally:

```yaml
- name: Install Linux system dependencies
  if: runner.os == 'Linux'
  run: sudo apt-get install -y libxcb-render0-dev ...
```

## Secrets

- Never hardcode signing credentials, API keys, or tokens.
- Use GitHub Actions Secrets (`${{ secrets.KEY_NAME }}`).
- macOS signing certificates must use a secrets-based approach (base64-encoded cert).

## Release Workflow Notes

- See `release.yml` for the existing release automation.
- Release builds should run on all three platforms before tagging.
- Binaries must be stripped (already configured in `[profile.release]` in `Cargo.toml`).
